</section>

<section class="section section--tight" id="where-it-fits">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Where it fits</p>
      <h2>One step in the pipeline you already run</h2>
      <p>Point Decoy at files or object storage, describe the transform in YAML, and ship the output wherever lower environments read from. Nothing is sent to us. Nothing is inferred silently.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flow" data-flow role="list">
      <div class="flow-step flow-step--edge" role="listitem"><strong>Source</strong><span>CSV, Parquet, fixed-width, S3, GCS, Postgres snapshot</span></div>
      <div class="flow-step" role="listitem"><strong>Scan</strong><span>STORM profiles every column and flags likely PII</span></div>
      <div class="flow-step" role="listitem"><strong>Subset</strong><span>Pull a small slice with every foreign key intact</span></div>
      <div class="flow-step" role="listitem"><strong>Mask or generate</strong><span>23 strategies, 34 providers, keyed and deterministic</span></div>
      <div class="flow-step" role="listitem"><strong>Validate</strong><span>Residual PII, FK parity, distribution checks</span></div>
      <div class="flow-step flow-step--safe" role="listitem"><strong>Evidence</strong><span>Hashed manifest of what ran, never raw values</span></div>
      <div class="flow-step flow-step--edge" role="listitem"><strong>Target</strong><span>Local, S3, GCS, your dev and test databases</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="small muted" style="margin-top: var(--space-4)"><a class="link-arrow" href="/how-it-works/">See the full walkthrough {% icon "arrow-right" %}</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="two-ways">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">One engine, two ways to run it</p>
      <h2>Built for the developer at the keyboard and the team that has to prove it</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-2" data-reveal>
      <article class="card card--door">
        <div class="icon-badge">{% icon "terminal" %}</div>
        <h3>{{ site.products.cli }}</h3>
        <p>The whole engine in one command. Scaffold a pipeline, scan a file, run it, and gate CI on the exit code. No server, no account, no telemetry.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>{% icon "check" %} 23 masking strategies, 12 generation types, 34 synthetic providers</li>
          <li>{% icon "check" %} Keyed, deterministic masking so joins survive across tables and runs</li>
          <li>{% icon "check" %} FK-aware subsetting and STORM PII detection</li>
          <li>{% icon "check" %} Six stable exit codes, JSON output, evidence manifests</li>
          <li>{% icon "check" %} Free and source-available (BUSL-1.1) on an Apache-2.0 engine</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="link-arrow" href="/cli/">Explore the CLI {% icon "arrow-right" %}</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card card--door">
        <div class="icon-badge">{% icon "layout" %}</div>
        <h3>{{ site.products.platform }}</h3>
        <p>A self-hosted web app on the same engine for teams that share pipelines, review findings together, and need an audit trail they can hand to a reviewer.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>{% icon "check" %} {{ site.products.builder }}: a visual builder and job history for every run</li>
          <li>{% icon "check" %} Tamper-evident, hash-chained audit log with export</li>
          <li>{% icon "check" %} Four roles, OIDC single sign-on, scoped API keys</li>
          <li>{% icon "check" %} S3-compatible storage, GCS, and Postgres sources</li>
          <li>{% icon "check" %} One Docker Compose deploy on your own host, air-gap capable</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="link-arrow" href="/platform/">Explore the Platform {% icon "arrow-right" %}</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight" id="proof">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="grid grid-3" data-reveal>
      <div class="stat">
        <div class="stat-value"><span data-count="1040000" data-format="m">1.04M</span></div>
        <div class="stat-label">rows per second per hashed column on the native kernel</div>
        <div class="stat-note">x86-64 Linux, single dev host; about 2.5x pandas wall-clock</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat">
        <div class="stat-value"><span data-count="100000000" data-format="m">100M</span></div>
        <div class="stat-label">rows masked in about seven minutes within 450 MB</div>
        <div class="stat-note">hash strategies, 8 threads, one host</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat">
        <div class="stat-value">0</div>
        <div class="stat-label">orphaned rows after subsetting, by policy</div>
        <div class="stat-note">composite and self-referencing keys supported</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="small muted" style="margin-top: var(--space-5)">Every figure comes from a published run with its conditions. <a href="/how-it-works/#performance">How we measure</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="why">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Why Decoy</p>
      <h2>Safe data you can reason about</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-2" data-reveal>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="icon-badge">{% icon "key" %}</div>
        <h3>Deterministic by construction</h3>
        <p>Every keyed strategy derives its output from your secret and the source value with HKDF-SHA256. Same input, same output, in every table and every run, so foreign keys and historical joins still line up.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="icon-badge">{% icon "file" %}</div>
        <h3>Explicit, reviewable YAML</h3>
        <p>The pipeline is a file you can diff, review, and version. STORM suggests a strategy per column and leaves a review comment; it never decides for you.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="icon-badge">{% icon "shield" %}</div>
        <h3>Evidence, not promises</h3>
        <p>Each run can write a manifest with the pipeline hash, file fingerprints, and row counts, and a residual-PII check that fails the build with exit code 4. The platform adds a hash-chained audit log.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="icon-badge">{% icon "server" %}</div>
        <h3>Your infrastructure only</h3>
        <p>There is no hosted control plane. The CLI runs where you run it; the platform is one Compose stack on your host. The only outbound calls are the ones you configure.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

